---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../../../assets/christian-dirnhofer.jpg';
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { routePath } from '../../../i18n/routes';
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  current="contact"
  title="Contact — Christian Dirnhofer"
  description="About Christian Dirnhofer and how to reach him."
  altHref={routePath('contact', 'de')}
>
  <div class="shell contact">
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <Image
      src={portrait}
      alt="Christian Dirnhofer"
      width={180}
      height={180}
      class="portrait"
      loading="eager"
    />
    <p>Email is quickest. I usually reply very fast.</p>
    <ul class="links">
      <li>
        <span class="mono-label">Email</span>
        <a href="mailto:christian@dirnhofer.net">christian@dirnhofer.net</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="mono-label">LinkedIn</span>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/christian-dirnhofer-a89b4a229/">
          christian-dirnhofer
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="mono-label">GitHub</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/Dirnei">Dirnei</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <section class="about">
      <h2>About me</h2>
      <p>
        I am a developer from Bavaria. It started roughly around 2007 with websites:
        HTML, CSS, PHP. From there via VB.NET and Java to C# in 2010. That one became my
        constant companion and is, rightly, my field today. Between Visual Source Safe
        and today's Azure DevOps I have seen and used all of it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Embedded came along in 2012. Plenty of Arduinos first, until the ESP32 turned
        up. Etching boards had to happen too. A breadboard is no good permanently and
        stripboard is too boring. I never quite got away from the embedded side of
        things. The longest and most ambitious project is the{' '}
        <a href="https://cloud.dartomat.com">Dartomat</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        When 3D printing got boring during the covid lockdown I quickly built myself a
        CO2 laser. Design, parts list, ordering, assembly and calibration. A three month
        project that taught me a great deal. It still runs, and so does the 3D printer.
      </p>
      <p>
        DevOps was a constant companion as well, in use everywhere all the time. In 2022
        infrastructure as code came along and got me hooked. At home there is Proxmox,
        Docker, Kubernetes, Ansible and Terraform. My home network is likewise
        completely over the top and set up more cleanly than that of most companies I
        have worked for.
      </p>
      <p>
        If it can be automated, I automate it. In real life, and in games even more so.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-block: 2rem 1rem;
  }
  .portrait {
    display: block;
    width: 180px;
    height: auto;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .contact p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .links {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .links li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-soft);
    padding-block: 0.75rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr;
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .links a:hover {
    color: var(--red);
  }
  .about {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }
  .about h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 1rem;
  }
  .contact .about p {
    color: var(--text-body);
  }
  .about a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    text-decoration-color: var(--hairline);
  }
  .about a:hover {
    color: var(--red);
    text-decoration-color: var(--red);
  }
</style>
